WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.135 --> 00:00:18.008
(birds squawking)

00:00:18.008 --> 00:00:20.564
- [Man] I knew a few light
keepers when there were all kinds

00:00:20.564 --> 00:00:22.814
of lighthouses around here.

00:00:24.611 --> 00:00:28.109
My father-in-law was a lighthouse
keeper on Brier Island.

00:00:28.109 --> 00:00:29.992
They started closing
them up, closing them up,

00:00:29.992 --> 00:00:31.399
and people just started disappearing.

00:00:31.399 --> 00:00:34.111
Some people went to other ones,

00:00:34.111 --> 00:00:35.584
and some people just stopped,

00:00:35.584 --> 00:00:39.731
but I think this one was
offered to a few people.

00:00:39.731 --> 00:00:41.430
Not very many took it.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:42.263
So.

00:00:44.655 --> 00:00:46.777
Well, I get up a-quarter-to-two
in the morning.

00:00:46.777 --> 00:00:48.802
Nice thing about here
is, you step out of bed,

00:00:48.802 --> 00:00:50.441
you're at work.
(laughs)

00:00:50.441 --> 00:00:53.050
Halifax coastguard radio,
Halifax coastguard radio,

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.685
this is Machias Seal
Island, Machias Seal Island,

00:00:55.685 --> 00:00:57.518
gen one nine, come in.

00:01:03.044 --> 00:01:05.382
There's always something to keep you busy,

00:01:05.382 --> 00:01:07.557
but you don't have a timetable
saying you have to get up

00:01:07.557 --> 00:01:10.027
this morning and do this,
or you have to do that,

00:01:10.027 --> 00:01:12.299
so you pretty well pick and
choose what you wanna do,

00:01:12.299 --> 00:01:13.633
when you wanna do it,

00:01:13.633 --> 00:01:17.300
when you can handle
what it is you're doing.

00:01:28.882 --> 00:01:30.848
One shift is 2 A.M. to 10 A.M.,

00:01:30.848 --> 00:01:32.426
and other shift is two in the afternoon,

00:01:32.426 --> 00:01:34.259
’til 10 in the evening.

00:01:36.702 --> 00:01:39.332
I feel now that, instead

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.365
of being the keeper of the light out here,

00:01:41.365 --> 00:01:44.050
you’re more of keeper of the island,

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:45.856
and looking after it

00:01:45.856 --> 00:01:50.023
as opposed to just the mechanical
systems that are on it.

00:01:56.171 --> 00:02:00.268
You're only bored out here if
you wanna be bored out here.

00:02:00.268 --> 00:02:01.266
If you're gonna be bored out here,

00:02:01.266 --> 00:02:03.849
you're gonna be bored anywhere.

00:02:04.886 --> 00:02:06.443
You just take a walk outside and look.

00:02:06.443 --> 00:02:07.655
There's always different birds to see,

00:02:07.655 --> 00:02:10.112
there's always something
different going on.

00:02:10.112 --> 00:02:11.457
You know, you look around,

00:02:11.457 --> 00:02:13.437
and if it wasn't for the 
houses and stuff here,

00:02:13.437 --> 00:02:17.604
you'd think it's the same as
it was 10 million years ago.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:21.203
(birds cawing)

00:02:27.341 --> 00:02:30.008
Pretty quiet in the winter time.

00:02:33.245 --> 00:02:36.482
The thrill of being out
here in a storm is nice.

00:02:36.482 --> 00:02:39.649
You can get some really nice pictures.

00:03:18.941 --> 00:03:20.989
I think one of the nicest
things is you come out here,

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:25.156
and you just kinda escape
from reality for a while.

00:03:26.376 --> 00:03:29.904
This is your little piece of reality,

00:03:29.904 --> 00:03:33.237
you make it whatever you want it to be.

